    "analytical_validity": "Eighteen samples with known genotype were studied and 100% concordance was obtained. Sanger sequencing analysis approaches an analytical sensitivity of almost 100%.",
    "clinical_validity": {
      "description": "It has been shown in Caucasians that C/T –13910 variant,  generates an increase in the synthesis of lactase, an enzyme that hydrolyzes lactose in the intestine. It has also been determined that C / G-13907 and T / G-13915 variants are associated with lactase persistence in African and Arab populations. The presence of the C/T-13910 variant in its homozygous form has a clinical sensitivity of 91.4% and clinical specificity of 96%.",
